---
import Layout from '@layouts/default.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Accessibility — Andrew Noblet"
  description="Accessibility features, appearance settings, and how to report an accessibility issue."
>
  <article class="editorial-page editorial-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h1 class="editorial-title">Accessibility</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="editorial-prose">
      <p>
        I aim to make this site usable with a keyboard, assistive technology,
        and different display settings.
      </p>
      <h2>Navigation and appearance</h2>
      <p>
        Use the “Skip to main content” link at the start of each page to bypass
        navigation. <a href="/settings">Accessibility settings</a> lets you change
        the theme, colors, and heading size.
      </p>
      <h2>Report a barrier or ask for another way to book</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:andrewbnoblet@gmail.com"
          >andrewbnoblet@gmail.com</a
        >. If you’re reporting a barrier, tell me which page you were on and
        what you were trying to do. If the booking calendar is hard to use, you
        can arrange a call by email.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
